{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-lepton-number-categorical","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:lepton-number-categorical","kind":"definition","title":"Categorical Lepton Number","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-beta-decay-skein"],"tags":["lepton-number","skein-relation","smoothing","conservation-law","categorical","weak-force"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.LeptonNumber","text":"lepton-number-categorical.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/lepton-number-categorical.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:lepton-number-categorical\"></a><p><strong>Lepton number</strong> is the count of Skein smoothings applied to the nuclear normal form.</p>\n<p><strong>Definition.</strong>\nLet <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{N}</code> be a nuclear link in Gröbner–Shirshov normal form. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{N}'</code> be obtained from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{N}</code> by a sequence of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code> Skein crossing changes. The lepton number of this transition is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L = k</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/lepton-number-categorical.md","heading":"Definition","number":"15.12.3"}
